CHS_TRANSLATION_PORTING_GUIDE.md - the method, written to be reused on a
different legacy BIOS: why the 504 MB limit exists, how to find the
relevant code in an unknown ROM, what to write, how to verify it, and the
full list of pitfalls (each one a bug that actually shipped here).

Project_Overview.md - status, drive results, what the patch does.
BIOS_Evaluation.md - root-cause analysis and the complete bug history
  (sections 3-7: one section per bug, with how it was diagnosed).
BIOS_ADDRESS_MAP.md - verified address map of this ROM.
Plan.txt - what is done and what is still open.

xlate_v5.asm - NASM source of the three translation routines
  (calc_factor, xlate_getparams, xlate_headcyl) spliced in at 0x76F5.
  CURRENT VERSION. v5 caps translated heads at 255 (16/32/64/128/255),
  computes logical cylinders as RealCyl*RealHeads/TransHeads in 16-bit
  math, preserves all 32-bit registers, never touches the caller's saved
  registers in the INT 13h frame, and only translates the functions that
  actually carry a CHS address.
build_v5.py - CURRENT build script: assembles xlate_v5.asm, asserts the
  original bytes at every patch site, splices the code in, patches the
  five sites, fixes the ROM checksum. Reads routine entry offsets from
  the nasm listing (xlate_v5.lst) instead of hard-coded constants.
SY019L1_27C512_CHSPATCH_v5.BIN - CURRENT ROM, confirmed on hardware.
  MD5 8e520e91100f932d3f054883b08d37da.

ide_harness2.py - Unicorn-based 16-bit real-mode harness. Loads either
  ROM, sets up a simulated IDE drive (optionally backed by sector data),
  BDA, IVT and CMOS, dispatches software interrupts, and runs real INT
  13h calls through the genuine dispatcher. Logs every task-file write
  with the resulting LBA, tracks the stack low-water mark, and can run
  the ROM's own INT 19h boot path. Known limitation: no PIC/interrupt
  modelling, so IRQ-driven waits run their slow worst-case path -- always
  compare against the original ROM under identical inputs rather than
  judging the patched ROM alone.
regress_v5.py - per-geometry regression: AH=08h geometry/DL/AL plus 44
  reads per geometry checked against the expected LBA (v4 vs v5).
boot_test.py - runs the ROM's INT 19h boot path against a simulated drive
  with an AA55 signature; shows whether the BIOS accepts the MBR.
verify_model.py - plain-Python re-implementation of the translation math.
analyze_bios.py - reproduces the verified ROM-structure facts.

BIOS_HEX.txt - the original ROM as a hex dump (build scripts rebuild
  orig.bin from it automatically).
BIOS_GHIDRA.txt - Ghidra disassembly of the original ROM (large).

